Product attribution and provenance
==================================

DRS OS is an original operating-system project built on top of the Android
Open Source Project (AOSP), https://source.android.com.

1. AOSP FOUNDATION
   DRS OS incorporates, and plans to incorporate, components of AOSP.
   AOSP source code is made available under its own license terms
   (predominantly the Apache License, Version 2.0, with Linux-kernel and
   some user-space components under GPL/LGPL and other permissive licenses
   as applicable). All upstream copyright notices, license texts, and
   attribution requirements are preserved and will be shipped with any
   future distribution of DRS OS. The upstream manifest commit used for any
   build will be recorded in the project decision log so that provenance
   can be audited.

2. TRADEMARKS
   Android is a trademark of Google LLC. This project references Android
   and AOSP solely to describe the upstream open-source foundation.
   DRS OS is an independent project: it is not affiliated with, endorsed
   by, sponsored by, or derived from the products of Google LLC, any
   device manufacturer, or any other third-party operating-system vendor.
   "DRS OS" and the DRS visual identity described under branding/ are
   original project branding.

3. BRANDING HYGIENE
   DRS OS will not present third-party developer brands, device-maker
   brands, or unrelated product brands in user-facing system surfaces.
   Where upstream AOSP strings or assets remain for functional reasons
   (for example, in code comments or build metadata), they are attributed
   to their origin and do not constitute DRS OS branding.

4. AI COMPONENTS
   DRS OS contains no artificial-intelligence components: no AI/ML models,
   no generative systems, no cloud AI APIs, and no AI assistant features.
   All product behavior is deterministic, rule-based, and local. This
   restriction is normative; see docs/decisions/ADR-0004-no-ai-policy.md.

5. THIRD-PARTY MATERIALS
   No third-party fonts, icons, images, or code are currently bundled in
   this repository. Future additions must be recorded in tools/README.md
   with license, source, and version information before inclusion.
   Candidate fonts and their licenses are documented in
   branding/typography.md; none are redistributed yet.

6. SIGNING MATERIAL
   This repository intentionally contains no private keys, certificates,
   or signing configuration. See docs/security/key-management.md.
